Build me a self-contained "Avatar Lab" — a local HTML playground for designing
a chat/AI-assistant avatar. Create a single file called `avatar-lab.html` with
NO build step and NO dependencies (pure HTML/CSS/JS, all inline). Then start a
local server (`python3 -m http.server 8088`) and open it so I can see it.

REQUIREMENTS:

1. FIVE avatar designs, shown together in a responsive card grid. Each is a
   pure-CSS animated avatar (no images, no Three.js):
   - "Orb"     — glossy radial-gradient sphere with two eyes, gentle float
   - "Reactor" — spinning conic-gradient energy rings around a bright core
   - "Blob"    — soft morphing droplet (animated border-radius) with eyes
   - "Bot"     — rounded robot head with a blinking face and an antenna
   - "Plasma"  — glassy orb with a blurred, spinning conic-gradient plasma fill

2. All five designs are driven by THREE CSS variables: --c1 (light), --c2 (glow),
   --c3 (deep). Changing the colors must recolor every design live.

3. A control bar at the top with:
   - 3 color pickers (light / glow / deep) wired to --c1/--c2/--c3
   - 6–8 one-click palette preset chips (e.g. mint, violet, sunset, ocean, gold,
